  "fit": "For each of the six training cases use the median of three counters separately per feature and the median of all six native CPU controls. Minimize the sum of squared relative errors with nonnegative coefficients and no intercept. Resolve equal losses in favor of the instructions-only solution when available. Use all six training cases regardless of native spread. There is no weight search or selection using the nine validation cases.",
  "validation_rule": "Score every individual observation against the native median of its case. A case passes if all three absolute relative errors are at most 20%. Report all nine validation cases and separately the native-stable subset. Report per-case native range and feature repeatability, median and worst errors, and probe CPU divided by mean native bracket CPU. Observed families have previous native timing data. This tests a prespecified feature choice on a known corpus.",
  "thresholds": {
    "min_native_ns": 20000000,
    "max_native_spread_ppm": 100000,
    "max_error_ppm": 200000
  },
